        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "What you need" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            { "name": "Lace weight yarn (white)", "qty": "80 m" },
            { "name": "3.5 mm crochet hook", "qty": "1" },
            { "name": "Tapestry needle", "qty": "1" }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Centre" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Make a magic ring. Round 1: ch 3, work 15 trebles into ring (16 trebles including ch-3). Join with a slip stitch." }]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Rounds 2 to 8 (increase pattern)" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Round 2: ch 5 (counts as tr, ch 2), *tr in next tr, ch 2; repeat from * around (16 ch-2 spaces). Round 3: ch 3, 2 tr in first ch-2 space, *3 tr in next space; repeat around. Rounds 4 to 6: continue with chain arcs between treble groups, adding 1 chain to the arcs each round. Round 7: work chain-5 arcs and 5-treble fans alternately around. Round 8: join each arc with a dc and work a picot at the tip of each fan." }]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": { "level": 2 },
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Finishing" }]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Fasten off and weave in the end with the tapestry needle. Block by pinning flat and misting with water." }]
      }
    ]
  }
